From 9fe1c99a61908c882c4dcb093c96bc90f23db281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:38:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Hand a signed-in person to the lesson room, and take
 Daily's word on what happened there

Three edge functions. room-ticket mints a two-minute single-use ticket
(hash stored, token in the URL fragment) after room_access names a seat;
room-redeem spends it behind a constant-time shared secret and turns it
into a magic-link sign-in for the same person; daily-webhook verifies
Daily's HMAC over the raw body and hands joins, leaves and endings to
import_lesson_room_facts, the one door that may write arrival and
departure onto a booking.

functions.yml deploys daily-webhook without JWT verification, like the
portal's doorbell, and warns (never fails) when the room's three project
secrets are missing. DEPLOYMENT.md section 2c says where each value comes
from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
