@@ -381,6 +381,96 @@ start around $50/month; Twilio Proxy is about $0.013/min plus ~$1 per number
 per month. In-app calls are the cheaper default, which is why they are listed
 first in the call menu.
 
+## 2c. The lesson room (room.mathvisionapp.com)
+
+Three edge functions carry the hand-off from the app to the room, and
+Daily's webhook back. Two of the secrets are shared with another system, so
+set the SAME value on both sides.
+
+```bash
+supabase secrets set ROOM_URL=https://room.mathvisionapp.com      # optional: edge_config.room_url is the fallback
+supabase secrets set ROOM_REDEEM_SECRET="$(openssl rand -hex 32)" # the same value goes in the room's Vercel env as ROOM_REDEEM_SECRET
+supabase functions deploy room-ticket
+supabase functions deploy room-redeem
+supabase functions deploy daily-webhook --no-verify-jwt
+```
+
+`--no-verify-jwt` on daily-webhook is required: Daily has no Supabase
+session and signs each delivery with its own HMAC, which the function
+verifies over the raw body and refuses when more than five minutes old. The
+other two keep JWT verification: room-ticket is called by the app with the
+person's own session, room-redeem by the room's server with the anon key as
+bearer plus an `x-room-secret` header compared in constant time.
+
+**Daily's webhook, once per Daily account (and once per project — staging and
+production each need their own).** There is no dashboard form; it is one REST
+call, and the `hmac` it returns is the secret:
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST https://api.daily.co/v1/webhooks \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $DAILY_API_KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{"url": "https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/daily-webhook",
+       "eventTypes": ["participant.joined", "participant.left", "meeting.ended",
+                      "recording.ready-to-download", "recording.error",
+                      "transcript.ready-to-download", "transcript.error"]}'
+# → {"uuid": "...", "hmac": "<base64>", "state": "ACTIVE", ...}
+supabase secrets set DAILY_WEBHOOK_SECRET='<the hmac field, exactly as returned>'
+```
+
+Deploy daily-webhook BEFORE the curl: Daily POSTs a test body to the URL and
+only creates the webhook on a 200. That ping has no event type and is
+answered without a signature (nothing is done with it). Every real delivery
+is refused until DAILY_WEBHOOK_SECRET is set — the function logs
+`daily-webhook has no DAILY_WEBHOOK_SECRET set` once — and Daily retries,
+then marks the webhook FAILED after repeated refusals.
+`curl https://api.daily.co/v1/webhooks -H "Authorization: Bearer $DAILY_API_KEY"`
+shows each webhook's state; a FAILED one is re-armed by deleting it and
+POSTing again (a new hmac, so set the secret again).
+
+Supabase → **Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs**: add
+`https://room.mathvisionapp.com/**`.
+
+**Check it took.** From the app, a confirmed online session in an enabled
+department shows "Join online session"; tapping it lands in the room signed
+in as the same person. Then:
+
+```sql
+select action, summary, created_at from public.audit_log
+ where action = 'lesson_ticket_redeemed' order by created_at desc limit 5;
+select session_id, opened_at, closed_at, transcript_status, provider_recording_id
+  from public.lesson_rooms order by created_at desc limit 5;
+```
+
+The first shows each redemption; the second shows Daily's events landing
+after a lesson (opened_at from the first join, closed_at from meeting.ended).
+
+### docs/RUNBOOK.md — new section after "## Pushes are not arriving"
+
+## The lesson room will not open, or a lesson's facts are not landing
+
+**From your phone:** "Join online session" shows an error, or opens the room
+on its sign-in page instead of the lesson. Everyone, or one person? Everyone
+is a secret or a deploy. One person is their seat: room_access names the
+assigned teacher, the student, an in-charge of the department, or an admin,
+for an online session that is confirmed or completed, from 15 minutes before
+it starts to 30 minutes after it ends, in a department whose room is on.
+
+**Developer:** Supabase → Edge Functions → logs, one function at a time.
+`room-ticket`: *the lesson room is not set up on the server* means neither
+ROOM_URL nor edge_config.room_url is set. `room-redeem`: *has no
+ROOM_REDEEM_SECRET set* — set it, no redeploy needed; a 401 means the room's
+Vercel ROOM_REDEEM_SECRET is not the function's; *ticket expired or used* is
+a two-minute ticket opened late or twice, and tapping Join again mints a new
+one. `daily-webhook`: *refused a … delivery: mismatch* means
+DAILY_WEBHOOK_SECRET is not the hmac of the webhook that is sending (staging's
+and production's differ); *no_secret* means it is unset; *stale* is a clock
+more than five minutes out. On Daily's side,
+`curl https://api.daily.co/v1/webhooks -H "Authorization: Bearer $DAILY_API_KEY"`
+— a webhook in state FAILED has stopped sending and is re-armed as in
+DEPLOYMENT.md §2c. A dead webhook loses the teacher's opened_at/closed_at and
+the recording and transcript status, not attendance: the student's own
+lesson_join writes arrived_at as well.
+
